out.push(box('Marking the unit check', [
  '**A  Language — 8 marks**, one each.',
  '**B  Listening — 6 marks**, one for each gap. ⚠ **Give the fourth mark only for both halves** — **that the only record is the corrected notes AND that the folder is by month rather than by supplier.** **The second half is the reason there is no figure, and the whole of her honesty about the range depends on it.**',
  '**C  Reading — 5 marks:** line 10 and what it does (2) · ⚠ **line 6 and what the bracket buys in March (2)** · ⚠ **line 5 quoted from memory (1)** — **and no mark for *because it was their idea*.**',
  '**D  Writing — 6 marks:** a testable standard with all three parts (3, one each) · ⚠ **the method naming who looks and from where (1)** · **a rejection quoting the line and the requirement (2).**',
  '**Total 25.** ⚠ **The profile to expect: A high, B split, C split, D high.** **B loses the fourth gap.** ⚠ **C loses on line 5, where learners give the credit to the idea rather than to the memory** — **and the point of the line is that it is performed, not that it is clever.** **D is usually strong, because by 14.6 the three parts have been written five times.**',
], C.lteal, C.navy));
out.push(note('Teacher\'s note. Four faults to watch, and the remedy for each. First, the stricter number. Every class believes a tighter tolerance is a better standard, and the remedy is one question asked repeatedly: what will the person actually do at six in the morning? A standard requiring an instrument nobody has to hand does not remove the judgement it was written against, it conceals it, and the page then contains a false claim about how the work is checked. Second, the missing sample. It is absent from almost every standard anybody brings, including good ones, and it is absent because nobody has ever told them a standard has a sample. Drill the three parts as a set and insist on the sample last, because it is the one that will be dropped. And refuse "at random" every time: it sounds rigorous, it means whichever one you pick, and the one a busy person picks is the one on top. Write a rule that chooses for them. Third, the rejection that describes the goods. Learners reject on description because the description is true and because it is how one speaks. The remedy is to make them find the clause in the other side\'s own document — which costs nothing, because the firm already has the document — and then to put the readings in and take the feeling out. Expect resistance to removing "we are very disappointed", and answer it with the question from the key: how many plates has that sentence ever produced? Fourth, and this is the one to spend the most time on: the standard stated after the work. Every text in 14.6\'s stage 7 will describe a standard applied retrospectively, and the point to land is that the same words before and after the work are two different documents, distinguished by nothing but a date and two signatures. Two notes on 14.7. The mediation only works if Nour asks what happens now before proposing anything, and a class that opens with the sheet never discovers the initialled correction — which exists, which is better than the sheet, and which is invisible unless somebody asks the open question first. And Hala\'s refusal to invent a yearly figure is worth as much as her finding: perhaps fifty, perhaps thirty, and here is why I cannot say. A range with its reason is a finding. A figure chosen to fill a gap is the figure that gets quoted back at you for a year, and it will be wrong.'));

if (require.main === module) L.build(out, process.argv[2], 'Proactive Business English B2 · Book 2 · Syria Edition · Unit 14 · Answer Key');
